caa817e3114dcfbd7613ed10","sourceKeyFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"243de460c01a135f05bfd98e1327686c5796bb07","sourceKeySHA256":"f09963466df7eb29bf00ef6cd1780235c0ce8a6fd53cbd3b3311e4c56cf7f91d","sourceKeyNumber":1,"sourceKeyFormat":"scanned-handwritten","bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-fourth-organic2022.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T01:39:45.422888Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":["Review the second handwritten alternative: the required isomer formula is C₄H₆Br₂."],"types":["Short answer"],"figures":0,"hash":"b2be22468cef28bccb7cea3d56f8d4be9b7510cdf2c88a737397b0bfd87c59dd"},{"id":"chemistry-fourth-organic2022-written-2","subject":"Chemistry","year":11,"examYear":2019,"units":"1","number":2,"source":"Organic Chemistry (Baldivis, 2019)","section":"Short answer","marks":8,"topics":["Chemical reactions","Organic chemistry"],"subtopics":["Formulae nomenclature and equations","Organic reactions and fuels"],"mixed":true,"text":"Write balanced equations for the reactions between the following substances: (You may like to use some of the space to start with a word equation but will only earn marks for the final balanced chemical equation) (8 marks) a. Propene and chlorine. b. Methane and bromine gas in UV light (first step only) c. but-1-ene and hydrogen chloride gas d. The combustion of propane gas in a plentiful supply of oxygen:","html":"<div><p>Write balanced equations for the reactions between the following\nsubstances:</p>\n<p><em>(You may like to use some of the space to start with a word\nequation but will only earn marks for the final balanced chemical\nequation</em>)</p>\n<p>(<strong>8 marks)</strong></p>\n<p>a. Propene and chlorine.</p>\n<p>b. Methane and bromine gas in UV light (first step only)</p>\n<p>c. but-1-ene and hydrogen chloride gas</p>\n<p>d. The combustion of propane gas in a plentiful supply of oxygen:</p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/5bb19a82cdd6821d851d190d.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 2, page 2\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"450696efbaa796aa19c04094e4b0dd32de5f3da6","sourceSHA256":"1b29fc3f3d0f4acf2535caf400195e45cb06e0b6caa817e3114dcfbd7613ed10","sourceKeyFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"243de460c01a135f05bfd98e1327686c5796bb07","sourceKeySHA256":"f09963466df7eb29bf00ef6cd1780235c0ce8a6fd53cbd3b3311e4c56cf7f91d","sourceKeyNumber":2,"sourceKeyFormat":"scanned-handwritten","bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-fourth-organic2022.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T01:39:45.422888Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":[],"types":["Short answer"],"figures":0,"hash":"b1916155100bdbcf01d05e3574163be8d71346fa7d0f3e3e9e8091a24987ce33"},{"id":"chemistry-fourth-organic2022-written-3","subject":"Chemistry","year":11,"examYear":2019,"units":"1","number":3,"source":"Organic Chemistry (Baldivis, 2019)","section":"Short answer","marks":7,"topics":["Chemical reactions","Organic chemistry"],"subtopics":["Formulae nomenclature and equations","Hydrocarbons isomers and nomenclature"],"mixed":true,"text":"Provide the full correct IUPAC name for each of structures 1–7