eight:auto\"></figure></div>","answerHtml":"<p><strong>Teacher review required.</strong> Guide’s printed structure (c) differs from the paper; the handwritten correction matches the paper’s alkene. Use the paper’s structure.</p><p>Structures 1–7 correspond to supplied key labels (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f) and (i), in order.</p><p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/a0b14387de19e1424b71399a.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 3, page 2\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/07815c3bae9d60d6f74d3edc.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 3, page 3\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure><p>For the corrected paper structure (c): <strong>1,1,2-trichloroprop-1-ene</strong>.</p>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"450696efbaa796aa19c04094e4b0dd32de5f3da6","sourceSHA256":"1b29fc3f3d0f4acf2535caf400195e45cb06e0b6caa817e3114dcfbd7613ed10","sourceKeyFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"243de460c01a135f05bfd98e1327686c5796bb07","sourceKeySHA256":"f09963466df7eb29bf00ef6cd1780235c0ce8a6fd53cbd3b3311e4c56cf7f91d","sourceKeyNumber":3,"sourceKeyFormat":"scanned-handwritten","bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-fourth-organic2022.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T01:39:45.422888Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":["Guide’s printed structure (c) differs from the paper; the handwritten correction matches the paper’s alkene. Use the paper’s structure."],"types":["Short answer"],"figures":7,"hash":"70ef055d262f106d9ecf80052fe9e7e6e01810ba3a524f1da309462360c713aa"},{"id":"chemistry-fourth-organic2022-written-4","subject":"Chemistry","year":11,"examYear":2019,"units":"1","number":4,"source":"Organic Chemistry (Baldivis, 2019)","section":"Short answer","marks":7,"topics":["Organic chemistry"],"subtopics":["Hydrocarbons isomers and nomenclature"],"mixed":false,"text":"Draw the structure of the following compounds: (7 marks) a. 2-methyl-3-ethyloctane b. trans-3-methylhex-3-ene c. Methylpropane d. 1,1-dichloroethane e. cis-hex-3-ene f. 2-chloro-4-methyloctane g. ethylbenzene","html":"<div><blockquote>\n<p>Draw the structure of the following compounds: <strong>(7\nmarks)</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>a. 2-methyl-3-ethyloctane</p>\n<p>b. <em>trans</em>-3-methylhex-3-ene</p>\n<p>c. Methylpropane</p>\n<p>d. 1,1-dichloroethane</p>\n<p>e. <em>cis</em>-hex-3-ene</p>\n<p>f. 2-chloro-4-methyloctane</p>\n<p>g. ethylbenzene</p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/145e8b5b9158e2a10c18cfa4.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 4, page 3\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/5480278eaf8b0297438e3d24.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 4, page 4\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"450696efbaa796aa19c04094e4b0dd32de5f3da6","sourceSHA256":"1b29fc3f3d0f4acf2535caf400195e45cb06e0b6caa817e3114dcfbd7613ed10","sourceKeyFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"243de460c01a135f05bfd98e1327686c5796bb07","sourceKeySHA256":"f09963466df7eb29bf00ef6cd1780235c0ce8a6fd53cbd3b3311e4c56cf7f91d","sourceKeyNumber":4,"sourceKeyFormat":"scanned-handwritten","bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-fourth-organic2022.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T01:39:45.422888Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":[],"types":["Short answer"],"figures":0,"hash":"43e6a0958c50ffd22aaf239dcb584791c39fcc5e0fc4e2ca2609f3d4242125db"},{"id":"chemistry-fourth-organic2022-written-5","subject":"Chemistry","year":11,"examYear":2019,"units":"1","number":5,"source":"Organic Chemistry (Baldivis, 2019)","section":"Short answer","marks":6,"topics":["Chemical reactions","Organic chemistry"],"subtopics":["Formulae nomenclature and equations","Hydrocarbons isomers and nomenclature"],"mixed":true,"text":"Each of the following compounds has been named incorrectly according to IUPAC. In each case describe the error(s) in naming, and write the correct name. (Hint: You will probably need to draw them) (6 Marks) a. 1,3-diethylpent-1-ene Description of error(s): Correct IUPAC name: b. 1,1-dichloro-2-bromobut-4-ene Description of error(s): Correct IUPAC name: c. trans-1,1-difluoroethene Description of error(s): Correct IUPAC name:","html":"<div><p>Each of the following compounds has been <strong>named\nincorrectly</strong> according to IUPAC.</p>\n<p>In each case <strong>describe</strong> the error(s) in naming, and\nwrite the correct name.</p>\n<p><em>(Hint: You will probably need to draw them)</em> <strong>(6\nMarks)</strong></p>\n<p>a. 1,3-diethylpent-1-ene</p>\n<p>Description of error(s):</p>\n<p>Correct IUPAC name:</p>\n<p>b. 1,1-dichloro-2-bromobut-4-ene</p>\n<p>Description of error(s):</p>\n<p>Correct IUPAC name:</p>\n<p>c. <em>trans</em>-1,1-difluoroethene</p>\n<p>Description of error(s):</p>\n<p>Correct IUPAC name:</p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/cc2649932a6d0f15bb6e5030.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 5, page 5\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"450696efbaa796aa19c04094e4b0dd32de5f3da6","sourceSHA256":"1b29fc3f3d0f4acf2535caf400195e45cb06e0b6caa817e3114dcfbd7613ed10","sourceKeyFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"243de460c01a135f05bfd98e1327686c5796bb07","sourceKeySHA256":"f09963466df7eb29bf00ef6cd1780235c0ce8a6fd53cbd3b3311e4c56cf7f91d","sourceKeyNumber":5,"sourceKeyFormat":"scanned-handwritten","bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-fourth-organic2022.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T01:39:45.422888Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":[],"types":["Short answer"],"figures":0,"hash":"853dac8821543f201aa78f17de0135f27d47401d13974ef8487a036668b0cf00"},{"id":"chemistry-fourth-organic2022-extended-6","subject":"Chemistry","year":11,"examYear":2019,"units":"1","number":6,"source":"Organic Chemistry (Baldivis, 2019)","section":"Extended answer","marks":8,"topics":["Chemical reactions","Chemical calculations","Organic chemistry","States of matter"],"subtopics":["Formulae nomenclature and equations","Moles mass and composition","Stoichiometry limiting reagents and yield","Organic reactions and fuels","Phase changes and physical properties"],"mixed":true,"text":"A portable gas stove that has become popular of late runs on aerosol-like cans of butane. These stoves use a combustion reaction between the butane and oxygen gas drawn from the surrounding air. a. Construct a balanced chemical equation for the complete combustion of butane. (2 marks) b. If, while boiling a kettle, 1.00 moles of butane were consumed, how many moles of Oxygen gas were required to be drawn from the air? (1 mark) c. What is the Molar mass of butane? (1 mark) d. During another cooking event, 150.0g of butane was burnt completely. i. How many moles of butane is this? (1 mark) ii. What mass of oxygen is required to complete this reaction? (3 marks)","html":"<div><p>A portable gas stove that has become popular of late runs on\naerosol-like cans of <strong>butane</strong>.</p>\n<p>These stoves use a combustion reaction between the butane and oxygen\ngas drawn from the</p>\n<p>surrounding air.</p>\n<p>a. Construct a balanced chemical equation for the complete combustion\nof butane. (2 marks)</p>\n<p>b. If, while boiling a kettle, 1.00 moles of butane were consumed,\nhow many moles of Oxygen gas were required to be drawn from the air? (1\nmark)</p>\n<p>c. What is the Molar mass of butane? (1 mark)</p>\n<p>d. During another cooking event, 150.0g of butane was burnt\ncompletely.</p>\n<p>i. How many moles of butane is this? (1 mark)</p>\n<p>ii. What mass of oxygen is required to complete this reaction? (3\nmarks)</p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p><strong>Teacher review required.</strong> Matching butane calculation is numbered 8 in the supplied key and 6 in the paper.</p><p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-fourth/0bfb075068391398df655af1.webp\" alt=\"Supplied handwritten marking key question 6, page 6\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"450696efbaa796aa19c04094e4b0dd32de5f3da6","sourceSHA256":"1b29fc3f3d0f4acf2535caf400195e45cb06e0b6caa817e3114dcfbd7613ed10","sourceKeyFile":"4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/Safety Bay/2022/4-Yr 11 Organic Chemistry test-solutions.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"243de460c01a135f05bfd98e1327686c5796bb07","sourceKeySHA256":"f09963466df7eb29bf00ef6cd1780235c0ce8a6fd53cbd3b3311e4c56cf7f91d","sourceKeyNumber":8,"sourceKeyFormat":"scanned-handwritten","bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-fourth-organic2022.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T01:39:45.422888Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":["Matching butane calculation is numbered 8 in the supplied key and 6 in the paper."],"types":["Extended answer"],"figures":0,"hash":"7b862de86e2c27804d1979a24d55ba0ba28bb010e027dbe9d4fd2c43f271324c"}]